# Auto-push to Git

After making any code or project changes in this repository:

1. Stage relevant files (`git add`)
2. Commit with a concise message explaining why
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push`)

Do this automatically at the end of each completed change set. Do not wait for the user to ask.

Skip only if there is nothing to commit, or if the user explicitly says not to push.
